---
import SectionHeading from "./CaseSectionHeading.astro";
import MediaFrame from "./ProductMediaFrame.astro";
import MerchandisingSystemGraphic from "./MerchandisingSystemGraphic.astro";
import originalSpreadsheet from "../assets/merchandising/graphics/merch-original-spreadsheet.png";
import screenshotHistory from "../assets/merchandising/graphics/merch-screenshot-history.png";
import currentTimeline from "../assets/merchandising/graphics/merch-current-timeline.png";

const capabilities = [
  "Promotion timeline",
  "Product-launch lane",
  "Email schedule",
  "Brand-specific views",
  "Year-over-year comparison",
  "Searchable planning information",
  "Homepage screenshot history",
  "Controlled spreadsheet editing",
];
---

<div class="merch-quick">
  <section id="overview">
    <SectionHeading number="01" eyebrow="Overview" title="A shared operating view for information that already existed." />
    <p class="ownership">I created and built the merchandising operations tool end to end.</p>
    <p class="section-intro">I owned opportunity identification, requirements with merchandising, UX/UI, application development, data presentation strategy, permissions and editing workflows, testing, and iteration.</p>
    <div class="overview-context">
      <div><span>Status</span><strong>Live and actively used</strong></div>
      <div><span>Source of truth</span><strong>The existing Google Sheet</strong></div>
      <div><span>Primary users</span><strong>Merchandising and teams across the business</strong></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="problem">
    <SectionHeading number="02" eyebrow="The problem" title="The data was available, but it was not easy to use." />
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-intro">The spreadsheet technically contained the information everyone needed. But for people outside the teams closest to it, promotions, launches, email activity, homepage content, paid media, and historical plans were difficult to interpret.</p>
        <p>Design, paid media, marketing, and leadership still had to ask merchandising or email teams for answers that were already in the sheet. The problem was information access and operational visibility, not the spreadsheet itself.</p>
      </div>
      <MediaFrame label="Original planning spreadsheet">
        <img src={originalSpreadsheet.src} width={originalSpreadsheet.width} height={originalSpreadsheet.height} alt="Original merchandising planning spreadsheet with dates and rows for products, homepage content, email, promotions, and related activity." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </MediaFrame>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="built">
    <SectionHeading number="03" eyebrow="What I built" title="A visual, searchable way to understand the operating plan." />
    <p class="section-intro">The application reads from the existing spreadsheet and turns the planning data into views people can understand and use without knowing how the sheet is organized.</p>
    <ul class="capability-grid">
      {capabilities.map((capability) => <li>{capability}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <div class="proof-views">
      <MediaFrame label="Current promotion and launch timeline">
        <img src={currentTimeline.src} width={currentTimeline.width} height={currentTimeline.height} alt="Current Merchandising Operations timeline showing promotions, product launches, and scheduled emails." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </MediaFrame>
      <MediaFrame label="Homepage screenshot history">
        <img src={screenshotHistory.src} width={screenshotHistory.width} height={screenshotHistory.height} alt="Historical homepage screenshots organized by date for planning and creative reference." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </MediaFrame>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="impact">
    <SectionHeading number="04" eyebrow="Impact" title="Operational visibility became a shared capability." />
    <div class="impact-grid">
      <div><span>Daily use</span><strong>Merchandising uses the tool as an operating view.</strong></div>
      <div><span>Self-service</span><strong>Teams can find common planning information without starting another handoff.</strong></div>
      <div><span>Ongoing leadership use</span><strong>The tool is used to present merchandising plans to the VP of Marketing.</strong></div>
      <div><span>Historical record</span><strong>Past homepage creative is available for year-over-year planning.</strong></div>
    </div>
    <p class="estimated-impact"><strong>Approximately 10–20 minutes of back-and-forth removed from common information requests.</strong><span>Estimated operational improvement; not a measured time study.</span></p>
  </section>

  <section id="why">
    <SectionHeading number="05" eyebrow="Why it worked" title="The source of truth already worked." />
    <blockquote>Keep the system of record. Redesign how people experience it.</blockquote>
    <p class="section-intro">Some upstream data already flowed into the Google Sheet. Replacing it would have created another system to maintain and another source that could drift out of sync. The better systems decision was to preserve the sheet and build a clearer experience on top of it.</p>
    <MerchandisingSystemGraphic />
    <div class="deep-dive-cta">
      <div><p>Extended reading</p><h3>Explore the source-of-truth decision, information architecture, write-back workflow, historical record, and roadmap.</h3></div>
      <button class="button-link" type="button" data-deep-toggle aria-controls="deep-dive" aria-expanded="false"><span data-deep-toggle-label>Read the Deep Dive</span> <span data-deep-toggle-icon aria-hidden="true">↓</span></button>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .merch-quick > section { padding-block: var(--space-8); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-height) + var(--space-7)); }
  .ownership { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); font-size: var(--step-2); font-weight: 680; line-height: 1.25; }
  .section-intro { margin: 0 0 var(--space-5); color: var(--color-text-soft); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .overview-context { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-top: var(--space-6); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .overview-context div { display: grid; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .overview-context div:first-child { padding-left: 0; }
  .overview-context div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .overview-context span, .impact-grid span { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .overview-context strong { font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .problem-grid { display: block; }
  .problem-grid p:last-child { color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .problem-grid :global(.media-frame) { margin-top: var(--space-6); }
  .capability-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin: var(--space-6) 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); list-style: none; }
  .capability-grid li { padding: var(--space-3); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .capability-grid li:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 0; }
  .capability-grid li::before { margin-right: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-accent); content: "—"; }
  .proof-views { display: grid; gap: var(--space-6); }
  .impact-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .impact-grid > div { display: flex; min-height: 10rem; flex-direction: column; padding: var(--space-5); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .impact-grid > div:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 0; }
  .impact-grid strong { margin-top: auto; padding-top: var(--space-5); font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.3; }
  .estimated-impact { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.58fr) minmax(0, 0.42fr); gap: var(--space-5); margin: 0; padding: var(--space-5); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 5%, transparent); }
  .estimated-impact span { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: var(--step--1); }
  blockquote { margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); padding-left: var(--space-4); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); font-size: var(--step-2); font-weight: 680; line-height: 1.25; }
  .deep-dive-cta { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-6); margin-top: var(--space-7); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .deep-dive-cta p { margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .deep-dive-cta h3 { max-width: 32rem; margin: 0; }
  .deep-dive-cta .button-link { flex: 0 0 auto; }
  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .overview-context, .estimated-impact { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .overview-context div { padding-inline: 0; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
    .overview-context div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    .deep-dive-cta { align-items: stretch; flex-direction: column; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .capability-grid, .impact-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .capability-grid li, .impact-grid > div { border-right: 0; }
  }
</style>
